WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
21 February 2024.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:07.070
Missak and Mélinée Manouchian
enter the Pantheon.

3
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:11.870
Missak was an Armenian poet who
had survived the 1915 genocide.

4
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.190
In Paris, he led an armed
group of immigrants.

5
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:20.670
On 21 February 1944, 22
men of his group were shot.

6
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.710
A German poster called
them foreign criminals:

7
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:28.790
«l'Affiche rouge». Only a small minority
of French people joined the Resistance.

8
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:32.000
So why does it matter
so much to France today?

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.160
In this mission, you'll map the
movements and «le maquis» across France.

10
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.010
Then you'll follow Jean Moulin,

11
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.160
code names «Rex», then «Max».

12
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.290
Your mission: explain why
so few came to mean so much.
